from pathlib import Path
root = Path('src/content/wiki/en/guides')
common = ' This guide uses the supplied 1.0 launch material and labels launch-period player observations as reference rather than official balance data.'
pages = {
 'tips': ('NMRIH2 Tips Guide for New Players','NMRIH2 tips guide for new players: squad positioning, noise control, inventory, ammunition unloading, doors, navigation, infection awareness, and 1.0 player references.','/images/3.webp','The safest new-player habit is to stay with the main squad, limit avoidable noise, share what the group needs, and choose extraction over a fight that consumes resources.',['New Player Guide: stay with the squad|Follow the main group rather than the fastest player or an isolated route. The supplied 1.0 player reference says the main squad improves communication, resource sharing, and mutual cover.','Noise and movement Tips|Routing around zombies and avoiding needless noise can save ammunition, health, and time. Vehicles are only temporary protection because zombies can climb them; some environment objects can buy the team time.','Inventory and ammunition Guide|Backpacks have weight and capacity limits, so carry what supports the current objective. Hold U to unload ammunition from a weapon when you need the rounds elsewhere.','Navigation and interaction Tips|Press C to check the compass direction and current objective. Player testing says white and reinforced doors can be kicked open while blue doors and iron grates cannot.','Combat awareness Guide|A downed zombie that still makes sound may rise again. Player testing also describes shove and kick behavior, but this is launch-period reference, not a timing guarantee.'],['/infection','/weapons','/maps']),
 'infection': ('NMRIH2 Infection Guide','NMRIH2 infection guide covering player-observed coughing, visual effects, hallucinations, pills, Gene Therapy, team communication, and Early Access version caution.','/images/4.webp','Infection is a core risk alongside extraction and permanent character loss. The supplied 1.0 player reference treats coughing, visual anomalies, and hallucinations as warning signs worth communicating.',['Infection Warning Signs Guide|The supplied materials identify coughing, visual abnormalities, and auditory hallucinations as infection signals. A 1.0 player test specifically describes a tentacle-like screen-corner effect.','Pills and Gene Therapy Wiki|Player testing describes pills as slowing infection and Gene Therapy as treating it. The folder does not document exact stages, timers, drop locations, or treatment conditions.','Team Communication Guide|If you suspect infection and cannot deal with it immediately, report it to the team. A squad that knows the risk can plan medicine, cover, and extraction.','Early Access Warning|An EA-era source says bites infect a Responder and untreated infection can turn that character hostile. As of 1.0 launch, may differ: this older account is not a complete current ruleset.','Reduce avoidable pressure|Avoid unnecessary noise, manage close contact, and maintain room for an exit. The supplied sources support infection importance but not a complete prevention formula.'],['/tips','/characters','/solo']),
 'crossplay': ('NMRIH2 Crossplay Guide','NMRIH2 crossplay guide for PC, PS5, and Xbox Series X|S, explaining full platform interoperability, eight-player co-op context, and unsupported assumptions to avoid.','/images/1.jpg','No More Room in Hell 2 supports full crossplay across PC, PS5, and Xbox Series X|S at the 1.0 launch, allowing squads to form across those platforms.',['Crossplay Wiki: supported platforms|The supplied official-summary material states full crossplay across PC, PS5, and Xbox Series X|S. It specifically supports PC-to-PS5, PC-to-Xbox, and PS5-to-Xbox combinations.','Eight-Player Co-op Guide|The game’s core cooperative mode supports up to eight players. Crossplay makes platform choice less restrictive for forming a squad.','What crossplay does not prove|Crossplay does not automatically establish cross-progression or cross-save. The materials do not explain friends, opt-out settings, voice interoperability, account transfer, or save syncing.','Squad Setup Tips|Confirm that each teammate has the current game version, then use the in-game social flow. Check platform privacy and online subscription requirements before assuming a feature failed.','1.0 release context|Crossplay arrived with Armageddon 1.0 and the console launch on 2026-08-11. Settings and restrictions can change through platform updates.'],['/ps5','/xbox','/release-date']),
 'ps5': ('NMRIH2 PS5 Guide','NMRIH2 PS5 guide covering the 2026-08-11 console launch, $29.99 reference price, PC and Xbox crossplay, 60 FPS target context, and troubleshooting limits.','/images/5.jpg','No More Room in Hell 2 launched on PS5 on 2026-08-11 with Armageddon 1.0. The supplied material records a $29.99 US launch reference and crossplay with PC and Xbox.',['PS5 Release Guide|PS5 received the game with the 1.0 Armageddon release on 2026-08-11, the series’ first console launch according to supplied material. Launch reference prices are US$29.99, €29.99, and £24.99.','PS5 Crossplay Wiki|PS5 players can form squads with PC and Xbox Series X|S players. The source does not document cross-save, progression transfer, party-code steps, or privacy exceptions.','Performance Reference Guide|A player review says the console release targeted 60 FPS and mentions dynamic or resolution scaling. This is a reported target, not verified stable PS5 performance or a graphics-mode list.','Troubleshooting basics|Keep the game updated, check online connection and privacy permissions, then test crossplay with a current-version squad.','What to expect|Treat PS5 as a supported 1.0 platform with crossplay, then rely on current PlayStation Store and in-game information for local price and performance details.'],['/crossplay','/xbox','/1.0-update']),
 'xbox': ('NMRIH2 Xbox Guide','NMRIH2 Xbox guide for Xbox Series X|S: 1.0 console launch, $29.99 reference price, Play Anywhere claim, online multiplayer subscription, and crossplay context.','/images/5.jpg','No More Room in Hell 2 supports Xbox Series X|S with the 1.0 console launch. The supplied material records PC and PS5 crossplay, a $29.99 US price reference, and online multiplayer requirements.',['Xbox Release Guide|Xbox Series X|S received the game with Armageddon 1.0 on 2026-08-11. The supplied launch reference lists US$29.99 and a 20 percent launch discount; prices can vary by region and time.','Xbox Crossplay Wiki|Xbox can play with PC and PS5 through the 1.0 crossplay feature. This supports broader eight-player co-op, but the supplied material does not establish cross-save or cross-progression.','Play Anywhere and subscriptions|The materials describe Xbox Play Anywhere and say online multiplayer needs a subscription. They do not identify a tier, so use the current Microsoft Store listing.','Performance reference|A player review describes console performance as targeted at 60 FPS and says Series S can reach HD resolution. These are reference-level claims, not measurements or guarantees.','Before joining a run|Update the game, confirm online access, check privacy settings, and ensure the squad is on a compatible current version.'],['/crossplay','/ps5','/1.0-update']),
 'review': ('NMRIH2 Review: 1.0 Launch Status','NMRIH2 review covering the 1.0 launch status, Mixed Steam reception snapshot, Early Access concerns, an 8/10 player reference, and console issue context.','/images/4.webp','As of the supplied 2026-08-15 snapshot, Steam reception is Mixed. Early Access criticism focused on performance, melee feel, animation, and matchmaking, while 1.0 brought positive discussion.',['Review Snapshot Guide|The supplied review snapshot records Mixed Steam reception at roughly 49 percent positive and 51 percent negative. This is a dated snapshot, not a permanent score.','Early Access Feedback Wiki|The source groups Early Access criticism around performance, optimization, melee handling, animation, and matchmaking. These points are review context, not universal claims about every 1.0 platform experience.','What 1.0 changed|Armageddon added Survival Mode, Raven Rock, Solo Training, tutorial content, consoles, crossplay, perk changes, and difficulty adjustments.','Player 8/10 Reference|One short player video gives the game 8/10, praising co-op tension, looting, objectives, and permanent character loss, while criticizing modes, progression, cosmetics, and long-term goals.','Console issue context|The material mentions optimization, controller deadzone, and settings persistence feedback, but does not provide a verified issue count or full hotfix history.'],['/1.0-update','/ps5','/steam-charts']),
 'release-date': ('NMRIH2 Release Date Guide','NMRIH2 release date guide: Early Access began on 2024-10-22, Armageddon 1.0 launched on 2026-08-11, and PS5/Xbox console release arrived with 1.0.','/images/5.jpg','No More Room in Hell 2 entered Early Access on 2024-10-22 and released Armageddon 1.0 on 2026-08-11, ending an approximately 22-month Early Access period.',['Release Date Wiki|Early Access began on 2024-10-22. The 1.0 release arrived on 2026-08-11 with Armageddon. The supplied material describes roughly 22 months between releases.','Armageddon 1.0 Guide|Armageddon marks the transition out of Early Access. Its listed content includes Survival Mode, Raven Rock, Solo Training, tutorial, crossplay, console support, perk changes, and difficulty adjustments.','Console Release Guide|PS5 and Xbox Series X|S received the game with 1.0, described as the series’ first console release. PC remains supported through Steam and Epic.','Price context|The supplied standard US price is $29.99. Check active platform stores for regional prices and current promotions.','Time-zone limits|The source supports release dates, not exact regional unlock times or a complete platform synchronization statement.'],['/1.0-update','/ps5','/xbox']),
 '1.0-update': ('NMRIH2 Armageddon 1.0 Update Guide','NMRIH2 Armageddon 1.0 update guide for Survival Mode, Raven Rock, Solo Training, tutorial, consoles, crossplay, weekly assignments, perks, and difficulty changes.','/images/5.jpg','Armageddon 1.0 released on 2026-08-11 and moved No More Room in Hell 2 out of Early Access. Its supplied feature list includes new modes, maps, console support, and system changes.',['Armageddon 1.0 Wiki|Armageddon ends Early Access and adds or expands Survival Mode, Raven Rock, Solo Training, tutorial content, PS5 and Xbox support, and full crossplay.','New Modes and Maps Guide|Survival uses Flooded, Lighthouse, and Night of the Living Dead. Raven Rock is the sixth Objective map. Solo Training provides practice without normal progression or permanent character loss.','Progression and Economy Guide|The materials list Weekly Assignments, Credits, Merits, expanded customization, and Rescue Beacon. Exact live values are not supplied.','Perks, combat, and difficulty|Reloading perks were added, three older perks were removed, and reroll cost was reduced. The material also reports broad melee, firearm, ammunition, sprint, shove, and difficulty adjustments.','Reset and launch context|The supplied source says certain pre-1.0 account, Credit, and Responder progression was reset while Early Access rewards were not.'],['/survival-mode','/perks','/release-date']),
 'difficulty': ('NMRIH2 Difficulty Levels Guide','NMRIH2 difficulty levels guide for Beginner, Normal, Hard, and Nightmare, including sourced 1.0 distinctions, rewards context, and limits on exact values.','/images/4.webp','No More Room in Hell 2 has four difficulty levels: Beginner, Normal, Hard, and Nightmare. The supplied material supports broad differences, not a complete table of live numerical values.',['Difficulty Levels Wiki|The four listed levels are Beginner, Normal, Hard, and Nightmare. Beginner is aimed at new players, Normal is standard, Hard increases pressure, and Nightmare is the highest setting.','Beginner and Normal Guide|The homepage material says Beginner was formerly Casual, with lower zombie health, UI prompts, and timed revives. It says Normal allows revives after the main objective.','Hard and Nightmare Guide|Hard is described as tighter on resources and higher in enemy pressure. Nightmare is described as less UI, stronger zombies, scarcer resources, and more special zombies.','Rewards and risk|The material says XP and Credit rewards differ by difficulty, but gives no multipliers. Choose a setting the squad can finish consistently.','What is not documented|No source in the folder provides precise health, spawn, ammunition, revive, or reward values for each level.'],['/tips','/solo','/survival-mode']),
 'steam-charts': ('NMRIH2 Steam Charts and Player Count','NMRIH2 Steam charts guide covering the approximate 11K Early Access peak, 2026 pre-1.0 monthly records, ownership estimates, and why live player counts are not hard-coded.','/images/1.jpg','Steam Charts','Steam player counts change continuously, so this guide does not hard-code a live number. The supplied snapshot records an approximate 11K Early Access Steam peak and pre-1.0 monthly context.',['Steam Charts Wiki|A displayed live count becomes stale quickly, so use SteamCharts or SteamDB directly for current Steam activity. Steam numbers do not represent Epic, PS5, Xbox, or full crossplay population.','Historical Peak Guide|The supplied SteamCharts material records an approximate 11,000 Early Access historical peak. It does not include a 1.0 release-day comparison.','2026 Monthly Context|The material records averages of roughly 130 in April, 1,001 in May during an event, 210 in June, and 157 in July. Those months are before 1.0 and cannot measure Armageddon performance.','Owners and estimates|SteamDB and player-count figures in the supplied material are estimates rather than an official ownership announcement.','Read trends carefully|The source has no August 2026 average, release-day peak, first-week retention, or complete post-1.0 series.'],['/review','/release-date','/1.0-update']),
}
for slug, entry in pages.items():
  title, desc, image, summary, sections, links = entry[-6:]
  if len(desc) < 140: desc += common
  body=[f'![No More Room in Hell 2 guide]({image})','']
  for s in sections:
    h,t=s.split('|',1); body += [f'## {h}',t,'']
  body += ['## Related Articles',*[f'- [Read Guide]({x})' for x in links]]
  front=f'''---\ntitle: "{title}"\ndescription: "{desc}"\ncategory: guides\ndate: 2026-08-15\nlastModified: 2026-08-15\nimage: {image}\ntags: ["nmrih2", "{slug}", "guide"]\nsummary: "{summary}"\nauthor: "NMRIH2 Wiki"\n---\n\n'''
  (root/f'{slug}.mdx').write_text(front+'\n'.join(body)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
